  "description": "After a KERI 2.0 inception, a binary-domain attachments group holds a generic list (-J) of three Bytes values of 6, 5 and 4 bytes, with codes 4B, 5B and 6B. In the binary domain each code's size counts triplets, so each value's end follows from its size and its lead bytes from its selector. The 6B table's text conflicts with itself about its pad size, as in CESR-0060.",
